---
title: Sequence Diagram — AI support chatbot (real-time, Server-Sent Events)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant W as ChatWidget (React)
    participant P as protect + chatLimiter
    participant C as controllers/chat
    participant DB as MongoDB
    participant L as utils/llm
    participant G as Gemini API

    U->>W: type a question and press Send
    W->>W: show the message + typing indicator
    W->>P: POST /api/v1/chat {messages: last 10 user/assistant turns}
    alt not logged in
        P-->>W: 401 (widget refreshes the token once and retries)
    else more than 10 messages in a minute
        P-->>W: 429 + Retry-After
    end
    P->>C: chat(req, res)
    C->>C: parseMessages(): roles user/assistant only, ≤ 1000 chars, last turn = user
    alt invalid (e.g. an injected "system" turn)
        C-->>W: 400 Bad Request
    end
    C->>DB: hotels + bookings WHERE user = req.user
    DB-->>C: public hotel data + only this user's bookings
    C->>C: buildSystemPrompt(): rules + DATA (treated as data, not instructions)
    C-->>W: 200 Content-Type: text/event-stream
    C->>L: streamChat({system, messages, signal})
    L->>G: streamGenerateContent?alt=sse (API key stays on the server)
    loop each chunk while the model is generating
        G-->>L: data: {candidates[0].content.parts[].text}
        L-->>C: text delta
        C-->>W: data: {"delta": "..."}
        W->>W: hide typing indicator, append text
    end
    C-->>W: data: {"done": true}
    Note over C,G: if the user closes the chat or 30 s pass,<br/>the request to Gemini is aborted (no wasted quota)
    W-->>U: complete answer, no page refresh
